  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently VRChat bans users with disabilities who use alternative input devices under the guise of using \"automated input\". This harmfully excludes a significant portion of the population who can't use standard controllers. Please work with accessibility experts and create methods to safely allow these sorts of uses in ways that won't disrupt the experience of other users. See this discussion on the problem. https://twitter.com/Firr/status/1507783289410568194\n\"Learned last night that two people I set up with the face tracker to movement software were banned from VR chat for using mods.\nIt was literally just emulating a controller. Now people without full use of hands aren't able to participate in VR with friends.  Really disappointing.\nFor the record, I do not know the whole story. As far as I'm aware this didn't break the ToS since this was just an alternate gamepad and a separate application that overplayed in VR space.  It did do some trickery to make the turn speed more useable but that was it.\"",
